      "message": "Gemini review:\n\n----\n### 1. Functional \u0026 Logic Issues\n\n**Critical: Event Re-triggering on Combined Masks**\nIn `common/host_event_commands.c`, the logic used to prevent infinite printing loops when setting or clearing events is flawed for combined masks:\n\n```c\nif (!IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_HOSTCMD_CONSOLE_EVENT) ||\n    (mask !\u003d EC_HOST_EVENT_MASK(EC_HOST_EVENT_CONSOLE_LOGS)))\n\tHOST_EVENT_CPRINTS(\"event clear\", mask);\n```\n\nIf `mask` contains multiple event bits (e.g., `EC_HOST_EVENT_CONSOLE_LOGS` *and* `EC_HOST_EVENT_BATTERY`), the condition `mask !\u003d EC_HOST_EVENT_MASK(EC_HOST_EVENT_CONSOLE_LOGS)` evaluates to `true`. \nThis will trigger `HOST_EVENT_CPRINTS`, generating a new console log. That log will subsequently trigger `host_set_single_event(EC_HOST_EVENT_CONSOLE_LOGS)`. Consequently, if the AP attempts to clear the console log event simultaneously with another event, the EC will immediately re-set the console log event.\n\n* **Remediation:** Instead of checking for exact equality, mask out the console log event from the print output so that other events are still printed, but the console log event itself never triggers a print.\n\n```c\nhost_event_t print_mask \u003d mask;\nif (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_HOSTCMD_CONSOLE_EVENT)) {\n\tprint_mask \u0026\u003d ~EC_HOST_EVENT_MASK(EC_HOST_EVENT_CONSOLE_LOGS);\n}\n\nif (print_mask) {\n\tHOST_EVENT_CPRINTS(\"event set\", print_mask); // Or \"event clear\" / \"event clear B\"\n}\n```\n\n**Unread Logs During Sleep**\nIn `zephyr/shim/src/console_buffer.c`, if a log occurs while the AP is suspended (`wake_host \u003d\u003d false`), the event is suppressed. If no subsequent logs are generated after the AP wakes up (`POWER_S0`), the AP will not receive a notification for the logs generated during sleep. \n* **Recommendation:** Verify if this is intended behavior. The AP typically polls `EC_CMD_CONSOLE_READ` upon wake anyway, so this is likely acceptable, but it should be explicitly documented in the commit message or code comments.\n\n### 2. Testing\n\n**Unmocked USB Suspend State in Tests**\nIn `zephyr/test/drivers/default/src/console.c`, `test_buf_notify_event` correctly forces the AP power state to `POWER_S0` to ensure the host event is allowed. However, it does not mock or enforce the USB suspended state:\n\n```c\n#ifdef CONFIG_EC_HOST_CMD_BACKEND_USB\n\tif (usb_is_suspended()) {\n\t\twake_host \u003d false;\n\t}\n#endif\n```\n\nIf the testing environment defaults to USB being suspended, `usb_is_suspended()` will return `true`, `wake_host` will be `false`, and the host event will never be set, causing the test to silently fail or timeout.\n* **Remediation:** Add logic to the test to explicitly set or mock the USB state to active/awake, similar to how you handled `power_set_state(POWER_S0);`.\n\n### 3. Code Style \u0026 Readability\n\n**Header Inclusion**\nIn `zephyr/shim/src/console_buffer.c`, you included `\u003csubsys/usbd_service.h\u003e` to access `usb_is_suspended()`. In the ChromiumOS EC codebase, this function is traditionally declared in `usb_hw.h` or `usb_api.h`. Verify that `\u003csubsys/usbd_service.h\u003e` is the correct Zephyr-native abstraction for this check, as bleeding subsystem headers into the console shim can create modularity issues.\n\n**Unnecessary Parentheses**\nIn `common/host_event_commands.c`, the parentheses around the mask equality check are redundant and slightly clutter the conditional:\n```c\n/* Current */\n(mask !\u003d EC_HOST_EVENT_MASK(EC_HOST_EVENT_CONSOLE_LOGS))\n/* Suggested */\nmask !\u003d EC_HOST_EVENT_MASK(EC_HOST_EVENT_CONSOLE_LOGS)\n```\n\n**Variable Initialization**\nIn `zephyr/shim/src/console_buffer.c`, `new_console_log` is guarded by `console_write_lock` and correctly re-initialized to `false` in `uart_console_read_buffer_init()`. This is thread-safe, but as a minor optimization, you can group the global variable declaration with the lock it depends on to make the concurrency explicit:\n\n```c\nK_MUTEX_DEFINE(console_write_lock);\n#ifdef CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_HOSTCMD_CONSOLE_EVENT\nstatic bool new_console_log; /* Guarded by console_write_lock */\n#endif\n```\n\n----\n\nNot sure about the `Header Inclusion` and the `Unnecessary Parentheses` looks ok to me as-is.",
